# 5. Postman Random Test Data

The POST request can generate random test data.

### Pre-request Script

```javascript
const names = ["Ali", "John", "Sara", "Mike", "Emma"];

const name = names[Math.floor(Math.random() * names.length)];

const account = Math.floor(1000 + Math.random() * 9000);

const balance = Math.floor(Math.random() * 900) + 100;

pm.variables.set("customerName", name);
pm.variables.set("accountNumber", account.toString());
pm.variables.set("balance", balance);
```

### POST Body

```json
{
    "customerName": "{{customerName}}",
    "accountNumber": "{{accountNumber}}",
    "balance": {{balance}}
}
```

Every time **Send** is clicked, Postman generates new values.

Example:

```json
{
    "customerName": "Sara",
    "accountNumber": "2175",
    "balance": 781
}
```

